      "category": "ai",
      "title": "Stealing Reasoning Traces from Proprietary LLM APIs",
      "url": "https://stolen-thoughts.com/",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49257876",
      "score": 650,
      "comments": 291,
      "author": "quantumgarbage",
      "published": "2026-08-11T13:22:00Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Side-channel and prompt-injection techniques can extract hidden Chain-of-Thought (CoT) reasoning tokens from reasoning-focused LLM APIs like OpenAI o1.",
        "Extracted reasoning traces accelerate model distillation, allowing developers to train open-weights models on proprietary step-by-step logic at low cost.",
        "Mitigating trace leakage requires API providers to enforce strict CoT token masking, response obfuscation, and enhanced logit privacy controls."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/programming",
