      "score": 1,
      "comments": 0,
      "author": "var0xyz",
      "published": "2026-08-12T12:59:17Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Define explicit problem scopes and failure modes before writing code to prevent premature optimization and architectural technical debt.",
        "Practice active comprehension during implementation rather than blindly accepting AI-generated code snippets or unverified dependencies.",
        "Prioritize clear abstractions and self-documenting APIs to reduce cognitive overhead during asynchronous pull request reviews and maintenance."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "hackernews",
      "subsource": "news.ycombinator.com",
      "category": "security",
      "title": "Exploiting System Management Mode with a very long interrupt",
      "url": "https://github.com/xoreaxeaxeax/smiiiiiiiiiiiiiiii",
