      "score": 184,
      "comments": 78,
      "author": "WhiteDawn",
      "published": "2026-08-10T16:03:14Z",
      "bullets": [
        "SMI timing anomalies and prolonged interrupts can desynchronize execution states between the host OS kernel and x86 System Management Mode.",
        "Attackers leverage extended execution windows to trigger TOCTOU race conditions, corrupting protected SMRAM memory to gain Ring -2 privilege.",
        "Defending firmware requires strict SMI handler execution bounds, SMRR memory protections, and validating interrupt state transitions in UEFI BIOS."
      ]
    },
